<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila sees Feb oil price hike 13.94 centavo/litre.</title>
<headline>Manila sees Feb oil price hike 13.94 centavo/litre.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' Energy Regulatory Board (ERB) said it sees local petroleum prices rising by an average of 13.94 centavos per litre once full oil industry deregulation is implemented on February 8.</p>
<p>&quot;The oil companies will now have to pass on the 13.94 centavos rise to consumers since with full deregulation, the OPSF will be abolished,&quot; ERB Commissioner Edward Castaneda told Reuters on Saturday.</p>
<p>The OPSF (Oil Price Stabilisation Fund), a buffer fund which protected the local market from international price fluctuations, will be abolished after full deregulation.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
